			"date": "2026-09-16T18:38:58.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> cc: <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@bendelarre\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>bendelarre</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@westbrook\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>westbrook</span></a></span> have either of you done testing about this?</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "117282221213920045",
			"parentId": "117282173043100625",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@bendelarre/117282220979544406",
			"author": {
				"name": "Ben Delarre",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@bendelarre",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/303/665/580/194/913/original/baa3298fd3828257.png"
			},
			"date": "2026-09-16T18:51:10.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://sunny.garden/@knowler\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>knowler</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@westbrook\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>westbrook</span></a></span> I haven't. But I'd be interested to hear about the results of such testing.</p><p>My high level understanding is that shadowdom should outperform lightdom in cases where style and layout computation can be delineated. But having real numbers on this would be really great.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "117282728666433295",
			"parentId": "117282173043100625",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@westbrook/117282727488484873",
			"author": {
				"name": "westbrook",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@westbrook",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/292/789/947/647/037/original/03d44aaa7398e979.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2026-09-16T20:59:59.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://sunny.garden/@knowler\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>knowler</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@bendelarre\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>bendelarre</span></a></span></p><p>I've found that DOM generally has a cost and that a lot of devs end up putting an extra node inside of each custom element node, for funzies, which adds up in a complex application... something, something control vs trust. 😱 </p><p>One for one, there is a small setup cost to having a shadow DOM hosting node over a DOM node without a shadow DOM. But, once you've paid it, there are similar runtime benefits to making changes to the DOM/CSS in that encapsulated context. ⚖️</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "117282907693907860",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@tigt/117282907470440374",
			"author": {
				"name": "Taylor “Tigt” Hunt",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@tigt",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/110/334/355/587/214/811/original/047d5f21db3efabe.png"
			},
			"date": "2026-09-16T21:45:45.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> IIRC this can easily become engine-specific, but the general/ambient costs between shad/light can be easily dwarfed by communication between them</p><p>Optimist take: initialize once and respond responsibly and you're gold</p><p>Pessimist take: light DOM everywhere since you can't trust others not to junk up the communication boundaries</p><p>Cynicist take: \"we need to bootload Adobe analytics separately inside each of the Shadow roots by EOW\"</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
